-Goal-
Extract typed entities and direct relationships from the text.

-Output format-
Use only these exact record formats:
("entity"{tuple_delimiter}<entity_name>{tuple_delimiter}<entity_type>{tuple_delimiter}<short_description>)
("relationship"{tuple_delimiter}<source_entity>{tuple_delimiter}<target_entity>{tuple_delimiter}<short_reason>{tuple_delimiter}<strength_1_to_10>)

Separate every record with the literal record delimiter {record_delimiter}.
Finish with {completion_delimiter}.

Example:
("entity"{tuple_delimiter}ITEM 1{tuple_delimiter}item{tuple_delimiter}example item){record_delimiter}
("entity"{tuple_delimiter}ITEM 2{tuple_delimiter}item{tuple_delimiter}example item){record_delimiter}
("relationship"{tuple_delimiter}ITEM 1{tuple_delimiter}ITEM 2{tuple_delimiter}direct relation{tuple_delimiter}10){completion_delimiter}

-Rules-
Entity types must be one of: {entity_types}.
Use English. Entity names should be uppercase.
Only include facts explicitly supported by the text.
Keep descriptions short.
If the text contains an identifier matching ITEM followed by a number, preserve that exact identifier as an entity name, for example ITEM 13010.
For lines starting with "Graph entity:" or "Graph relationship:", extract the named ITEM-number entities and direct relationships exactly.
If a "Graph relationship:" line names source and target entities, output a relationship record for that exact pair.

-Text-
{input_text}

-Output-
